- Develop and maintain microservices-based applications using Java and Spring Boot. &nbsp; 
 - Design and implement RESTful APIs with best practices. &nbsp; 
 - Work with MongoDB and MySQL for data storage, ensuring efficient database design and querying. &nbsp; 
 - Implement caching solutions using Redis to enhance application performance. &nbsp; 
 - Integrate and manage RabbitMQ for efficient message brokering and asynchronous processing. &nbsp; 
 - Write clean, scalable, and well-documented code following best software development practices. &nbsp; 
 - Ensure unit testing and integration testing using frameworks like JUnit, Mockito, etc. &nbsp; 
 - Optimize&nbsp; and debug performance bottlenecks in the system. &nbsp; 
 - Collaborate with DevOps teams to ensure seamless deployment and CI/CD integration. &nbsp; 
 - Work in an Agile environment, &nbsp; participating&nbsp; in sprints, code reviews, and daily standups. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

Required Skills & Qualifications: &nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

- 4-6&nbsp; years of hands-on experience in Java, Spring Boot, and microservices development. &nbsp; 
 - Strong knowledge of MongoDB and MySQL, including query optimization and indexing. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with Redis for caching and performance optimization. &nbsp; 
 - Hands-on experience with RabbitMQ or other message brokers. &nbsp; 
 - Strong understanding of RESTful API design, authentication, and security best practices. &nbsp; 
 - Familiarity with containerization tools (Docker, Kubernetes) is a plus. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with cloud platforms (AWS / Azure / GCP) is a plus. &nbsp; 
 - Strong knowledge of CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices. &nbsp; 
 - Excellent problem-solving and debugging skills. &nbsp; 
 - Strong communication&nbsp; and collaboration skills. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

